hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7","[AI-translation] Abu Saeed Khudri se riwayat hai, farmate hain: Hum ek safar mein the, hum ne utar gaah kiya to ek larki aayi aur kahne lagi: Hamare deh ka sardar saanp ka dasta hua hai, aur hamare qaum ke log ghayab hain, to kya tum mein se koi raqi hai? To ek shakhs un ke saath khada ho gaya jise hum ruqya karne ke qabil naheen samajhte the, us ne usay ruqya ki to woh aadmi aafiya pa gaya, us ne us ke liye tees bakrian muqarrar kiya aur humein doodh pilaya. Jab woh wapas aaya to hum ne us se kaha: Kya tum ruqya karna jante thay ya tum ruqya karte thay? Us ne kaha: Naheen, main ne to sirf Umm-ul-Kitab ke siwa ruqya naheen ki. Hum ne kaha: Jab tak hum Nabi (sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ke paas na aayein ya na poochein, tum kisi se kuch mat kehna. Phir jab hum Madina pahunche to hum ne is ka zikr Nabi (sallallahu alaihi wasallam) se kiya, to aap (sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ne farmaya: Aur usay kya maloom ke yeh ruqya hai? Baant do aur mere liye ek hissa muqarrar karo."
"8","[AI-translation] Zaid se riwayat hai ke unhone Abu Salam ko kehete hue suna, kehte hain: Mujhe Abu Umamah Bahili ne hadees sunai, kehte hain: Maine Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ko farmate hue suna: Quran parho, beshak woh qayamat ke din apne saathiyon ke liye shafa'at karne aayega. Do noorani suraton (Zahrawain) ko parho, Surah Al-Baqarah aur Surah Aal-e-Imran ko, kyunke woh dono qayamat ke din aisi aayengi goya do badal hon, ya goya do siyah saaye hon, ya goya parindah ke do jhund hon jin ke par phaile hue hon, apne saathiyon ke liye hujjat karte hue. Surah Al-Baqarah parho, beshak isey lena barkat hai aur isey chhodna hasrat hai, aur batil log isey (apni jadugarse) hara naheen sakte."
"9","[AI-translation] Jubeer bin Nafeer se riwayat hai, farmate hain: Maine Nawwas bin Sam'an Kalabi ko kehete hue suna: Maine Nabi (sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ko farmate hue suna: Qayamat ke din Quran aur us ke ahl (jo is par amal karte the) laye jayenge, un ke aage Surah Al-Baqarah aur Aal-e-Imran pesh aayengi. Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ne un dono ke liye teen misaalein bayan farmayi jo main ne us ke baad kabhi na bhulay, farmaya: Goeya woh do badal hon, ya do siyah saaye hon jin ke darmiyan noor (roshni) ho, ya goya do jhund hon parindah ke jo par phaila kar hue hon, apne saahib ke liye hujjat karte hue."
